Here's the full analysis. Since you confirmed this runs on **every user-facing string** (hundreds per page), all findings are elevated to hot-path severity.

---

### Scan Execution Checklist

| Recipe | Hits |
|---|---|
| `.ToLower()/.ToUpper()` | 2 (L97, L103) |
| `.All()/.Any()` LINQ on char | 2 (L93, L101) |
| `params` array | 1 (L213) |
| `.Select/.Cast/.Aggregate` LINQ | 5 (L86-89, L171, L214) |
| `.Replace(` | 1 (L187) |
| `.Contains(string)` w/o comparison | 0 (L61 uses `char` — fine) |
| `.Split(` | 2 (L75, L158) |
| `.Substring(` / `[1..]` range slice | 1 (L106) |
| `GeneratedRegex` | 2 ✅ |
